## I2 · Write Path — `▶` all 8 domains wired and E2E verified (2026-08-05, §23)

### What's done

All mutation flows wired with real branches in `client.ts` + component handlers, E2E verified against the real deployed backend:

| Domain | Methods wired | Key patterns |
|--------|--------------|--------------|
| Service records | create, update, delete, submit, withdraw | Idempotency on submit; `withVersion` on update |
| Evidence upload | uploadIntent, uploadContent, complete, upload (convenience) | 3-step flow; raw PUT for binary |
| Review decisions | decide (approve/return/reject/escalate) | Idempotency; `recordVersion` in body |
| Account operations | adjust, reverse, freeze, unfreeze | Signed centi-coins; idempotency on adjust/reverse |
| Projects | create, update, publish, close, archive | `withVersion`; `ActionRequest { version }` on actions |
| Registrations | create, cancel, confirm, reject | Student is principal, not body field |
| Proposals | create, update, submit, withdraw, review | Field mapping (hours→min, goal→objective); idempotency |
| Notifications | markRead, markAllRead | PATCH/POST real branches |

### d8 completion

- User CRUD — `GET/POST/PATCH /users`, `POST /users/{id}/reset-password`; delete = deactivate (no DELETE endpoint)
- Import/export — template download, file upload → validate → commit/cancel; async export → poll → download
- Student profile edit — `PATCH /students/{id}` for profile fields; ledger fields shown read-only (record/account-derived)
- Feature flags — `toast.info('not available')` (no backend write endpoint)
- Rules — `api.rules.*` methods in client.ts ready; UI needs UX redesign (draft→publish vs in-place edit)

### Remaining I2 exit criteria (polish for I3)

- [ ] Validation errors → per-field display (mechanism built, rendering not wired)
- [ ] Conflict 409 → "refresh" UX (caught as toast, no refresh offer)
- [ ] Two-step flow display (proposal→project, review→credit shown in UI)
- [ ] Bulk action partial-failure per-row reporting
- [ ] Permission-aware affordances

